        texte "The server (`--cible serveur`) is generated separately, from the `serveur` block."
        soustitre "The Android application"
        texte "`--cible android` writes readable Kotlin: each page is a Compose function, its variables are state, and its events are functions that wait for the server without blocking the screen. Navigation goes through Navigation Compose, and Android's back button returns to the previous page. The icons are the same as on the web."
        code terminal :
            humalis compile taches.humalis --cible android --sortie taches-android --serveur https://api.mysite.com
        liste :
            texte "`memorisee` values stay on the device; `memorisee en secret` and the session go through a vault encrypted by the Android Keystore."
            texte "From the emulator, the computer is called `10.0.2.2`: a server started on `http://localhost:3000` is reached automatically. Otherwise only `https://` is allowed."
            texte "The application tabs are a bar at the bottom of the screen."
        texte "The whole language works on Android, as on Apple:"
        liste :
            texte "{accent "Languages and fonts"}: the application starts in the device's language when the site has it; `selecteur de langue` and `changer langue par …` change it. Theme fonts shipped as `.ttf` or `.otf` are loaded."
            texte "{accent "Navigation"}: sub-pages show inside their parent page, and a link to an anchor (`carte#desserts`) scrolls down to it. `liens profonds "magasin"` opens the application from `magasin://produit/42`; with `et domaine "…"`, `https://` links open it too: compile with `--empreinte` (the certificate's SHA-256 fingerprint, given by `keytool -list -v`) and publish the file written in `a-publier-sur-le-site/`."
            texte "{accent "Device"}: `photo dans …`, `scanner code dans …`, `position dans …`, `verifier identite` (fingerprint, face or the device code), `vibrer` and `signature dans …`. Each permission is requested the first time it is needed."
            texte "{accent "Files"}: `fichier "…" dans …` opens the system picker, `envoyer fichier …` follows its progress, `telecharger bon de …` and `telecharger … en csv` open or share the file."
            texte "{accent "Media"}: charts keep the web's colors, scales and “Voir les données” table; maps show OpenStreetMap tiles and their attribution; audio and video go through Android's player and never start on their own."
            texte "{accent "Account"}: invitations, account roles and fields, choosing a password from the link received, Google or Apple login, payment (Stripe's page opens in the browser), `demander a ia`, whose answer appears as it comes, and `activer notifications`, through Firebase Cloud Messaging (see “Notifications”)."
            texte "{accent "Real time and offline"}: `en direct`, `avec hors ligne`, `… hors ligne` sends (kept on the device, sent in order when the network returns) and `en arriere plan :` (run by the system about every quarter of an hour, when the network is there)."
            texte "{accent "Motion and keyboard"}: entrance animations and `effet leve` follow the device's “remove animations” setting. A list `avec deplacement` is reordered with a long press, then a drag; TalkBack offers “Move up” and “Move down” (named « Monter » and « Descendre »). With a keyboard attached, the page's shortcuts work. `menu de l'application` becomes the “⋮” menu at the top of the app, with its shortcuts."
            texte "{accent "Native components"}: `actualiser en tirant` becomes pulling the page down, `action en glissant` slides the row to the left, `menu d'options` opens on a long press (TalkBack offers these actions too) and `etat vide` shows its icon in the middle."
            texte "{accent "App forms"} (see “App-only forms”): the widget (Glance, refreshed by WorkManager and when leaving the app), received shares, opened files, the icon's shortcuts, the Quick Settings tile, the keyboard, the live activity (an ongoing notification with its progress, promoted on Android 16) and notification buttons. `sur montre` pages form a Wear OS module (`montre/`) and `sur tele` pages an Android TV module (`tele/`), driven by touch or by the remote. Voice commands go through Google Assistant's App Actions, which take no reply to speak: the app opens, shows the sentence and reads it aloud. System search stores the records in AppSearch, which the launcher may or may not show. Android Auto shows the list; Google must approve the app before it is published."
            texte "{accent "Sources"}: a source with a secret key goes through the server's gateway, with the session; the key never ships with the app."
        texte "CSS becomes Compose, rule by rule, when a rule targets a class (`.card { … }`): background, color, text size and weight, margins and padding, border, corner radius, shadow, width, and the gap between children. A `utiliser style "./android.css" sur android` stylesheet applies to Android only."
        soustitre "The Windows application"
        code terminal :
            humalis compile boutique.humalis --cible windows --sortie boutique-windows --serveur https://api.mysite.com
            cd boutique-windows
            dotnet build
            dotnet publish -c Release -r win-x64
        texte "The generated folder is a readable .NET 10 project in C# and WPF, not meant to be edited by hand. `dotnet publish` gives a single `.exe` file that contains .NET: nothing to install on the PC (`-r win-arm64` for an ARM PC). Building also works on a Mac or on Linux; only running it needs Windows 10 or 11."
        liste :
            texte "The look follows Windows 11 (Fluent theme), light or dark like the system; `changer theme par sombre` changes that choice, and it is kept."
            texte "One page at a time, with a Back button, `Alt+←` and the mouse's back button."
            texte "The Humalis server is called with the same session as the Apple application: the token is kept encrypted by Windows, readable only by the person signed in to the Windows session. `memorisee` goes to `%LOCALAPPDATA%`."
            texte "Several languages: the selector, `changer langue`, and numbers, prices and dates written the way the chosen language writes them; the choice is kept on the PC."
            texte "Charts, maps (OpenStreetMap tiles, or another provider with `tuiles`), audio and video with their transcript, QR codes, SVG images, choosing and uploading files, `sous page`, anchors and the application's tabs."
            texte "`partager …` copies the text (and the link) to the clipboard."
            texte "`en direct`: the list is read again when the server announces a change, as long as the page is open."
            texte "Animations and hover effects are not drawn yet; the compiler says so."
            texte "What Humalis cannot do yet is written in C#: `utiliser composant "Carte" sur windows "./natif/Carte.cs"`, with its NuGet libraries (`paquet windows "…" version "…"`); see \"A hand-written native view\"."
            texte "Not on Windows yet: payment, AI, signing in with Google or Apple, invitations, notifications sent by the server. Compilation stops and says which line needs them."
        texte "The app-specific forms work without an MSIX package: the app registers itself with Windows at each launch, for the signed-in person, without administrator rights. It only runs once: an opened file, a right-click or a notification button is passed to the window already open."
        liste :
            texte "`page "…" dans la barre du systeme`: an icon in the notification area. A click opens the page in a small window next to the icon; right-click offers Open and Quit. Closing the app's window hides it without stopping it."
            texte "`raccourcis de l'icone`: the jump list of the taskbar button."
            texte "`quand on ouvre un fichier`: the app appears in \"Open with\" for these extensions. Windows 10 and 11 let the person choose the default app."
            texte "`lancer au demarrage de l'ordinateur`: shown in Task Manager (\"Startup apps\"); `avec discret`, only in the notification area."
            texte "`quand l'utilisateur touche "…" dans une notification`: Windows notifications with their buttons; a button answers without opening the window."
            texte "`menu clic droit`: the File Explorer right-click. On Windows 11 the command is under \"Show more options\" (or Shift+F10), as for any unpackaged app."
            texte "`quand on partage vers l'application`: the Windows \"Share\" panel only accepts packaged (MSIX) apps. Without a package, the app is in the right-click \"Send to\" menu: `partage.fichier` is the file path, `partage.texte` the text of a `.txt`, `partage.lien` the address of an Internet shortcut. The compiler reminds you."
        texte "`Application.exe --desinstaller` removes everything the app registered: run it before deleting the `.exe` file."
        texte "Without code signing, Windows shows a warning (SmartScreen) on first launch: \"More info\", then \"Run anyway\"."
        soustitre "The Humalis rendering engine"
        texte "The website is produced by the Humalis engine: it is the default."
        code terminal :
            humalis compile site.humalis --cible web --sortie site
        texte "Each page is an HTML file already written by the compiler, which a small script picks up without rebuilding it. When a variable changes, only what reads it changes. The site can also be produced with React: write `--moteur react`, or once for a project in `humalis.projet.json`: `"moteur": "react"`; `humalis developper` and `humalis tester` use it too. A program that uses what the engine cannot do yet is produced with React: the compiler says why."
        texte "The desktop app also takes the engine's pages, one per address. It switches to React for a React component or a value `memorisee en secret`."
        texte "Modules (`utiliser module`), components (React, Vue, Svelte) and Web Components work the same way: the file is loaded only by the pages that use it. Anything shown after loading (data from the server, a component) is not in the initial HTML."
        texte "A click made before the page is ready is not lost: it is replayed as soon as the page is ready."
        texte "`pour chaque t dans taches avec animation :` makes rows slide when the list changes, and new rows fade in (unless the person asked for less motion). It works on the web: elsewhere the compiler says so and rows change without sliding."
        texte "#### Real time"
        texte "`en direct` keeps a page up to date when the server changes:"
        code humalis :
            page "commandes" :
                variable commandes = []
                titre "Commandes"
                quand la page se charge :
                    envoyer requete vers "commandes" dans commandes en direct
        texte "An order created elsewhere appears by itself, without a reload. The server only announces that something changed: the page then re-reads the normal route, with its access rules, so nothing private travels through this channel. It works on the web, on the desktop, on Apple, on Android and on Windows. After a connection loss, the page reconnects by itself and catches up with what changed. The `mobile` target (Expo) and static pages read the list once, and the compiler says so."
        texte "With a PostgreSQL database you can run several copies of the server: a change received by one is announced by all. Without PostgreSQL, keep a single copy. Changes close together are grouped, and pages do not all re-read at the same moment."
        texte "#### Reading the server at build time"
        texte "To have public pages carry their content in the HTML, give your server's address in `humalis.projet.json`:"
        code texte :
            { "principal": "site.humalis", "moteur": "humalis", "lireServeur": "https://api.example.com" }
        texte "Nothing is read unless you ask. Four rules always apply:"
        liste :
            texte "only `tout le monde peut lire` routes are read, never a restricted page;"
            texte "the read is anonymous: no key, no cookie;"
            texte "whatever comes from the server is written as text, never as code;"
            texte "the address uses https, and a redirect is not followed."
        texte "For a `source`, name each public route: `"lireSources": ["api/products"]`. A source that sends a key is never read."
        texte "Data removed from the server stays in the HTML until the next build: rebuild the site after an important deletion."
    sinon :
        texte "Le même fichier donne toutes les cibles. Quand une construction n'existe pas sur une cible, le compilateur le dit clairement au lieu de produire quelque chose de faux."
        tableau "web, statique, mobile, desktop, apple, android, windows" :
            colonnes " ", "web", "statique", "mobile", "desktop", "apple", "android", "windows"
            rangee "Pages, éléments, styles, thème", "oui", "oui", "oui", "oui", "oui", "oui", "oui"
            rangee "Ton propre CSS", "oui", "oui", "non (styles nommés seulement)", "oui", "en partie (règles d'une classe ; le reste est listé) ; au point près dans une page `dessinee pour`, `@media` et mode sombre compris", "en partie (règles d'une classe ; le reste est listé)", "en partie (règles d'une classe ; le reste est listé)"
            rangee "Requêtes vers un serveur", "oui", "oui", "oui", "oui", "oui", "oui", "oui"
